


The hstr_length function "hstr_length.h"

            The hstr_length function returns the length of
            the short string specified by the argument. The
            argument must provide access to a sequence of
            HSTR_SIZE_MAX characters. The hstr_end function
            behaves as if the { HSTR_INDEX_MAX }-th
            character of the sequence were a null character.
            Unlike the strlen function, the hstr_length
            function returns an int.
